## Day 72 Session Plan

### Task 1: `/fork` — Conversation Branching
Files: `commands_session.rs, dispatch.rs, help.rs`  
Why: Closes a genuine competitive gap vs Claude Code and Gemini CLI. We have /stash (push/pop) and /checkpoint (file snapshots), but no way to branch the conversation into parallel explorations. /fork <name> creates a named branch, /fork switch <name> switches between them. Built on the same save_messages/`restore_messages` API that stash uses.

### Task 2: Extract Testable Command Routing from `dispatch.rs`
Files: dispatch.rs  
Why: 766 lines, 0 tests — the REPL's traffic cop is completely untested. Extract a pure route_command() function that maps input strings to a CommandRoute enum, then add 15-20 tests. This strengthens our test moat (2,502 → ~2,520) and makes the routing logic verifiable without mocking agents.

### Task 3: Release Prep — 0.1.11
Files: Cargo.toml, CHANGELOG.md  
Why: 9 sessions since 0.1.10 (May 2). Major additions: prompt caching, desktop notifications, /copy, cache hit rate display, tool recovery hints, model pricing updates, multiple .ok() fixes. Enough for a point release. Version bump + changelog entry only — tagging is done by humans.

